# The repo root is the build context for both images (docker/*.Dockerfile),
# so without this file everything on disk enters the context -- including
# local apps/*/.env files, which then sit inside build-stage layers of every
# image built on this machine. Secrets never belong in a layer, cached or not.
#
# Kept deliberately narrow: the Dockerfiles COPY package manifests, packages/,
# apps/api, apps/web and docker/Caddyfile, so those paths must stay visible.

# Real environment files, wherever they live. The two tracked examples are
# documentation and carry no secrets, so they may stay.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Version control and agent state -- large, and none of it builds.
.git
.claude

# Installed and built locally; the image installs and builds its own.
**/node_modules
**/dist

# Documentation, CI and editor noise -- nothing in the images reads them.
docs
.github
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
